# Expansion of `MXX 0 1` via two ancilla qubits.
#
# Implements the joint XX measurement as:
#     RX 2
#     R  3
#     CX 2 3
#     CX 2 0
#     CX 3 1
#     MX 2
#     MX 3
#
# Wires are drawn in the order q_0, q_2, q_3, q_1 so the data-ancilla
# CXs (CX 2 0 and CX 3 1) are short, non-crossing vertical lines.
#
# Compile to SVG with:
#     qpic -f svg mxx.qpic       # writes mxx.svg
# or to TikZ for inclusion in LaTeX:
#     qpic -f tikz mxx.qpic > mxx.tex

# a W D1
# b W D2
# a b \rotatebox{90}{$M_{ZZ}$}

# a b END
=
a b START


a W a
b W b
c W \ket{0}
d W \ket{+}

# Bell pair on the ancillas.
c +d

# Stitch each ancilla to its data partner.
q2 +q0
q3 +q1

# Measure both ancillas in the X basis.
q2 M $X$
q3 M $X$


a W D1
b W D2
c W |0\rangle |0\rangle
a b G \rotatebox{90}{$ZZ^{\frac{1}{4}}$}

a b END
=
a b c START

a +c
b +c
c G $e^{i \theta Z}$

b +c
a +c